  "vendor_website": "presys.com.br",
  "description": "Precision thermometer for three resistance thermometers and three thermocouples, with RS-232 and RS-485 Modbus RTU",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Presys, Termometro de Precisao PT-511, Manual Tecnico",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Termometro de Precisao PT-511, Manual Tecnico",
      "url": "https://www.presys.com.br/downloads/manual_1_pt511.pdf",
      "note": "section 5.5, linked in issue #388"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Every register holds one byte (0 to 255). Values that need more are spread over consecutive registers, one byte in each, most significant byte at the lowest address, so they are listed here byte by byte and have to be put together by the reader. The document says the tool reads at most 10 registers per request.",
    "The numbers in the document are the addresses sent on the wire (its example reads registers 50 to 53 with start address 0x0032), so address_base is 0.",
    "Serial settings: 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, RTU, RS-232 or RS-485 (up to 31 instruments). The slave address is set on the instrument (menu COM). The document does not give a baud rate: 9600 and slave 1 are placeholders.",
    "Functions 3, 4, 6, 8 and 16 are supported. Not mapped: the probe tags (10 characters, one per register) and the mantissa and exponent registers of the calibration coefficients of each probe.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
